D6 is implemented except one item that needs a ruling. The driver has no public apply to put the deferred link-response cursor on a `:link-request` entry, so I stopped on that part as the brief says. The full report is at `collab/1791200000000-vm-engineer-ucf-d6-engine-r3.findings.md`.

**Open ruling:** the existing publics don't fit. `apply-observation` is poll-only, `apply-mint` replaces an unminted cell, and `apply-close` removes a close record. I added nothing and did not hand-assoc the cursor. The engine now builds the entry without `:cursor` and never scans or retries it under a gate. Until the Architect picks a mechanism, a gated link cannot complete.

**Changed files:** only `src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc`, `src/cljc/yin/vm/module.cljc` and `test/yin/vm/engine_gate_test.cljc`.

- **Gated link append:** `module/append-link-request` has a new `[resources entry gate]` arity that returns the entry unchanged with zero appends. The 2-arity stays, because `yin.vm.ucf.remote` mentions it.
- **Deferred cursor:** `require-handler` skips the `:dao.stream/newest` mint under any gate.
- **Child stamping:** a child gets `:yin.k/gate` and nothing else when it is created and before each run.
- **Install children:** in `:exporting` and `:ended` no child runs. A direct `resume-continuation` is refused in those two modes.
- **Gated sweep:** under any gate the sweep no longer retries link requests, scans link responses or reads FFI responses. It also no longer retries put/next in `:exporting` and `:ended`, which D5 had left open.

**Tests:** I added nine tests that run the whole zero-call list on all four kernels.

| Check | Result |
|---|---|
| New tests before the implementation | 60 failures, 3 errors |
| `yin.vm.engine-gate-test` after | 27 tests, 340 assertions, 0 failures, 0 errors |
| Focused `yin.vm` / `yin.repl` / `dao.stream` run | 1805 tests, 17419 assertions, 2 failures, 1 error |
| kondo on the three files | 0 errors, 0 warnings |

The 3 focused-run failures come from a missing `target/yin-repl.js` Node build (two) and a failed Dart peer compile (one). I didn't re-run them on a clean tree. CLJS, CLJD and cljstyle were not run.

**Gate completeness:** every path in the plan's list is covered by a zero-call row under `:running` and by refusal or inertness under the closed modes. Nothing in the diff still observes for a gated task. The one caveat is the link-cursor ruling above. I made no source change that sets `:yin.k/gate`.

**Coverage gaps:**
- Child-creation stamping is tested on the JVM only, because creation is reached only through link-response polling, which is now gated off.
- Direct resume is tested at the engine function that all four kernels call, not by driving each kernel.
That's the last of the expired monitors from the stopped run. No action is needed, and the report stands as written.
